    <article class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
        <h1>About ShedOS</h1>

        <p>
            ShedOS is a developer-first Linux distribution built on Arch. It
            ships a tuned Hyprland desktop, a working developer toolchain,
            and a rolling upgrade path that respects the files you've edited.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it exists</h2>

        <p>
            Most distributions choose between two tradeoffs: stable and
            opinionated, or rolling and DIY. The first pins you to old
            software; the second pins you to a hobby. ShedOS aims for the
            middle — current software, a working desktop on first boot, and
            one command to stay up to date.
        </p>

        <h2>What's in the box</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>Hyprland on Wayland, with waybar, mako, walker, and the shedos-screensaver lock.</li>
            <li>Neovim (LazyVim), VS Code, and Zsh preconfigured.</li>
            <li>Language runtimes for Python, Node, Go, Rust, and C++.</li>
            <li>Docker, Podman, and Kubernetes tooling ready on first boot.</li>
            <li>BTRFS with snapshots; LUKS encryption optional at install time.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Source and license</h2>

        <p>
            Source lives at
            <a href="https://github.com/theshedman/shedos">github.com/theshedman/shedos</a>
            and is GPL-3.0. Branding assets under <code>branding/</code> are
            not covered by that license — reach out before re-using them.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <ul>
